.TH THUMTOO 7 "2026-09-17" "thumtoo" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
thumtoo \- image cache and index library (overview and environment)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B thumtoo
is a
.B cache and index library
for image and document pixels. It is
.B not
an image viewer or file manager. Desktop applications such as biltoo open a
.B Client
against an on-disk
.B Store
and request sizes, soft previews, zoomable 256\(mu256 tile pyramids, archive
member listings, and optional user data (tags, sets).
.PP
Hosts link
.I libthumtoo
and include headers under
.IR <thumtoo/*.hpp> .
Command-line tools
.RB ( thumtoo-prepare ,
.BR thumtoo-status ,
.BR thumtoo-tile ,
.BR thumtoo-gc ,
.BR thumtoo-archive ,
.BR thumtoo-bench )
operate on the same Store layout.
.SS Client model
.TP
.B open
.BR thumtoo::Client::open ( cache_root , executor , workers , data_root )
opens (or creates) the Store under
.I cache_root
and optional user data under
.IR data_root .
.TP
.B get_*
Non-blocking SQLite reads. Safe to call from a GUI thread.
.TP
.B request_*
Enqueue work on a worker pool (default: hardware concurrency, capped).
Completion callbacks run on the
.B Executor
passed to
.BR open()
(GUI loop, main thread, or inline for CLI tools) \(em never directly from a
worker unless the Executor is inline.
.TP
.B Interest / tiles
Hosts publish which URIs are visible (interest). Tiles are 256\(mu256 cells;
scale 0 is full resolution; each +1 halves linear size (floor-half dimensions).
See
.IR TILES.md
in the source tree.
.SS Cache layout
Default durable cache root:
.IP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumtoo/
.br
or, if
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is unset,
.IR ~/.cache/thumtoo/ .
.PP
Typical contents (schema \(>= 100):
.IP
.I index.sqlite
\(em locators, media rows, tile coverage
.br
.I blobs/
\(em content-addressed payloads
.PP
User overlay (tags and related data) defaults to
.IR data_root
=
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/thumtoo/
(or
.IR ~/.local/state/thumtoo/ )
when
.B Client::open
is called with an empty
.IR data_root .
Hosts may still pass an explicit path.
.PP
The Store is always rooted at the cache directory itself (legacy nested
.I store/
layouts are migrated when present). Older environment switches such as
.B THUMTOO_STORE_ROOT
and
.B THUMTOO_STORE_ONLY
are ignored by current clients.
.SS URIs
Paths are stored as URIs (for example
.IR file:///path/to/image.jpg ).
Archive members use an archive URI form (see
.BR thumtoo-archive (1)
and
.BR thumtoo-status (1)
examples).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Boolean flags treat a non-empty value as on, except
.BR 0 ,
.BR false ,
and
.B no
(case-insensitive first letter) which are off.
.TP
.B THUMTOO_DEBUG
When on, the Client prints task traces to
.B stderr
and appends the same lines to
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumtoo/debug.log
(or
.IR ~/.cache/thumtoo/debug.log ).
Re-checked at runtime so a late
.B export
in the same process takes effect.
.TP
.B BILTOO_THUMTOO_DEBUG
Same effect as
.B THUMTOO_DEBUG
(host alias used by biltoo).
.TP
.B THUMTOO_DEBUG_OVERLAY
When on, enables debug overlay helpers (also accepted as
.BR BILTOO_DEBUG_OVERLAY ).
.TP
.B THUMTOO_DEBUG_APPEARANCE
When on, traces appearance/grade paths (also accepted as
.BR BILTOO_DEBUG_APPEARANCE ).
.TP
.B THUMTOO_DEBUG_ARCHIVE
When on, prints archive open / TOC / extract / visit lines to
.B stderr
(prefix
.BR thumtoo-archive: ).
Also enabled when
.B THUMTOO_DEBUG
is on. Useful for solid RAR timing without full Client task noise.
.TP
.B THUMTOO_MIRROR_ARCHIVES
When on, sequential extract may copy the archive once under
.I cache/archive_mirror/
before opening (default off).
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Parent of the default cache directory
.IR thumtoo/ .
CLI tools that take
.B \-\-cache
override this for that invocation only.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Default parent for
.I data_root
.RI ( user.sqlite
tags/collections) and appearance state when present; otherwise
.B HOME
.RI ( ~/.local/state ).
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Legacy location for
.IR user.sqlite ;
on open, a missing state-root file is migrated from here when present.
.TP
.B HOME
Fallback for cache and state paths when XDG variables are unset.
.PP
Build-time feature macros (not runtime environment), such as
.BR THUMTOO_HAVE_CURL ,
.BR THUMTOO_HAVE_MUPDF ,
and
.BR THUMTOO_HAVE_DJVU ,
select optional backends at compile time. Hosts may also test
.B THUMTOO_API_*
macros in
.I <thumtoo/client.hpp>
for API availability.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumtoo/
Default Store root (index, blobs, optional debug.log).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/thumtoo/
Default
.I data_root
.RI ( user.sqlite )
and appearance state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thumtoo-prepare (1),
.BR thumtoo-status (1),
.BR thumtoo-tile (1),
.BR thumtoo-gc (1),
.BR thumtoo-archive (1),
.BR thumtoo-bench (1)
.PP
